@startuml class-meta
title The translation layer — syn::Meta in, openings out

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package syn <<Frame>> {
  enum "syn::Meta" as Meta {
    Path(Path)
    List(MetaList)
    NameValue(MetaNameValue)
  }
  note bottom of Meta
    **This is the attribute AST.**
    Nothing here invents a node layer beside
    it — Meta already IS the set of shapes an
    attribute can be written in, and
    ""Punctuated<Meta, Comma>"" is its spine.
  end note
}

package "proc_macro_flow_traits::meta" <<Frame>> {

  enum "Opening<'ast>" as Opening {
    Path(PathOnly<'ast>)
    List(ListBody<'ast>)
    Value(ValueExpr<'ast>)
    --
    +shape_name() -> &'static str
  }

  class "PathOnly<'ast>" as PathOnly {
    +0: &'ast syn::Path
  }
  note right of PathOnly : nothing to parse —\npresence is the signal

  class "ListBody<'ast>" as ListBody {
    +0: &'ast TokenStream
    --
    +metas() -> Result<Punctuated<Meta, Comma>>
    +exprs() -> Result<Punctuated<Expr, Comma>>
    +is_empty() -> bool
  }
  note right of ListBody
    **UNPARSED.** ""MetaList::tokens"" is raw,
    which is what lets a terminal node choose
    ""exprs()"" instead of ""metas()"".

    ""bounds(0, 64)"" is impossible without it:
    a bare literal is not valid Meta at all.
    (#meta-vs-expr)
  end note

  class "ValueExpr<'ast>" as ValueExpr {
    +0: &'ast syn::Expr
  }
  note right of ValueExpr
    **UNPARSED**, and needs no parser of ours:
    ""MetaNameValue::value"" is already an Expr.
  end note

  interface Shape {
    +type Input<'ast>
  }
  note left of Shape
    A shape is not a tag we attach — it is
    WHICH OPENING the payload arrives through.
    That collapses two concepts into one, and
    is what makes ""#[shape(..)]"" checkable by
    rustc rather than by us.
    (#shape-is-the-opening)
  end note

  package "AttributeKind" <<Node>> {
    class MetaList <<unit struct>>
    class NamedValue <<unit struct>>
    class "Path" as PathMarker <<unit struct>>
  }
  note bottom of MetaList
    A **module of unit structs**, not an enum:
    a variant cannot be named in type position,
    and the selector has to be an ARGUMENT to
    ""#[shape(..)]"" rather than the attribute
    head (#no-path-head).
  end note
}

Meta --> Opening : From<&'ast Meta>
Opening *-- PathOnly
Opening *-- ListBody
Opening *-- ValueExpr

MetaList ..|> Shape
NamedValue ..|> Shape
PathMarker ..|> Shape

MetaList ..> ListBody : Input
NamedValue ..> ValueExpr : Input
PathMarker ..> PathOnly : Input

note as Recursion
  Each element of a ""ListBody::metas()"" is
  itself a ""Meta"", hence itself an ""Opening"".
  That is the whole recursion — the spine
  goes as deep as there are named nodes,
  and ""exprs()"" is where it stops.
end note

Recursion .. ListBody

note as Emit
  Every opening implements ""ToTokens"" and
  re-emits what it came from unchanged.
  The compiler-checked selector depends on
  that holding: ""#[shape(AttributeKind::MetaList)]""
  round-trips verbatim into a type position.
end note

Emit .. Opening

@enduml
